<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    
    <h2>What Is the Reese's® Peanut Butter Cup Blizzard® Treat?</h2>
    <p>The Reese's® Peanut Butter Cup Blizzard is the top choice for peanut butter and chocolate fans. Reese's PB cup pieces — the full candy, chopped — are blended throughout DQ soft serve so you get a combination of chocolate shell and peanut butter filling in every spoonful. It is richer and more calorie-dense than the <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo Blizzard</a> and substantially higher-calorie than the <a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard">Cookie Dough Blizzard</a> at the Large size.</p>
  <p>Find all Blizzard prices on <a href="/">The Dairy Queen Menu</a> or view the full <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard Treats</a> lineup.</p>

    <h2>Reese's Blizzard vs. Royal Reese's Blizzard</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/items/royal-reeses-blizzard">Royal Reese's® Blizzard</a> adds a warm peanut butter-filled center for approximately $1 more per size. If you are already a peanut butter lover, the Royal version takes the flavor intensity considerably higher. For guests who want to try the Reese's Blizzard for the first time, the standard version ($3.49 Mini) is the better starting point.</p>
  <h2>Calorie Warning — Large Is Significant</h2>
  <p>The Reese's Large Blizzard at approximately 1,210 calories is one of the highest-calorie single items on the entire DQ menu. It surpasses the <a href="/items/flamethrower-stackburger">FlameThrower Stackburger</a> at 780 cal and approaches the calorie count of a full <a href="/items/chicken-strip-basket-4pc">Chicken Strip Basket</a> meal. Order a Small or Mini if you are calorie-conscious.</p>

    <h2>How It Compares to Other Blizzards</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Flavor Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Reese's® PB Cup Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>600</td><td>Rich PB + chocolate, very high calorie</td></tr><tr><td>Oreo® Cookie Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>420</td><td>Cookie crunch, moderate calorie</td></tr><tr><td>Butterfinger® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>470</td><td>Lighter PB + chocolate option</td></tr><tr><td>Royal Reese's® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>620</td><td>Same + peanut butter center, ~$1 more</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>First timer?</strong> Order a Mini (3.49) — it's 4–5 spoonfuls, perfect for a taste test before committing to a full cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Best size for one person:</strong> Small (4.49) at 600 calories hits the sweet spot of satisfaction without going overboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Upgrade option:</strong> Ask to blend in a hot fudge swirl for richer chocolate depth, or add extra mix-ins (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Check the flip:</strong> DQ guarantees every Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down — if your crew doesn't flip it, it's free.</li>
    </ul>

